nd uses a fork to press down the sides  last but not least he takes butter and  smears it over the top  and adds a little bit of salt then he  bakes it to light golden brown  and there you have it andre 3000's quick  little apple pie  what is this it looks like a calzone i'm  nervous  this looks just like a mega sized apple  pie hand pie  i'm open-minded i'll give it a try  okay this one's interesting it's fine  the filling  it's just like clear gel definitely like  apple sauce inside  this is pop biscuits with apple sauce in  it  if i had to rate it out of 10 i'd  probably give it like a  three or four if i had like a side of  jam it would be good but otherwise i'm  not  too crazy about this one next up claire  sabbats  claire savas starts off by peeling and  coring her apples  bear with me guys this is a long recipe  then she cuts the apples into pieces  yeah i'm still cutting up apples here  she then adds sugar  cinnamon brown sugar and tosses it all  together  then she flowers her counter and rolls  out two pieces of dough that she made  the night before  she places both pieces on parchment  paper and puts it right into the fridge  she places apple cider into a medium  saucepan scrapes in the seeds of a  vanilla bean and throws in the pod  brings it to a boil to reduce it to two  thirds and then adds in the juice from  the apples she had set aside  then she removes the vanilla bean pod  and on the side stirs in corn starch  into  three tablespoons of water throws it  into the mixture  mixes it together until it forms a paste  then she adds the paste  back into the apples then she takes her  first pie crust  cuts off the excess dough and does a  quick egg wash  on the sides of the pie then she places  her apple pie mixture  into the pie crust and then claire puts  dollops of butter along the top of the  apples  then she takes the final pie crust and  places it on her pie dish  and does a quick egg wash off the top  this pie is going to get messy so she  places it